{
  "id": "q-81203",
  "parts": [
    {
      "part": "problem",
      "original_record": "before",
      "value": "If $U=\\{1,2,3,…,10\\}$ is the universal set and $A=\\{2,4,6,8,10\\},$ then the complement of $A$ is",
      "original_html_sha256": "40357bd1130ad8e4c577811327abc293df2be3dbd0089c90167aba9fb3998bd7",
      "extractor_sha256": "1591183da328a4140792793d2cc113fd535ab5f25bc7f284ceb1b6f251efad18",
      "source_file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071504/repairs/source-provenance-v2/structured-source/source/40357bd1130ad8e4c577811327abc293df2be3dbd0089c90167aba9fb3998bd7.html",
      "extraction_errors": []
    },
    {
      "part": "worked_solution",
      "original_record": "history",
      "value": "The complement of $A,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{A},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $A.$\n\nThe elements of $U$ that are not in $A$ are $1,$ $3,$ $5,$ $7,$ and $9.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $A$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{A}=\\{1,3,5,7,9\\}.\n$$",
      "original_html_sha256": "781bb63fcb7500ad9837d501759e5e7b79b4bc2ac6f2cc9b059cc80f8ec92179",
      "extractor_sha256": "1591183da328a4140792793d2cc113fd535ab5f25bc7f284ceb1b6f251efad18",
      "source_file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071504/repairs/source-provenance-v2/structured-source/source/781bb63fcb7500ad9837d501759e5e7b79b4bc2ac6f2cc9b059cc80f8ec92179.html",
      "extraction_errors": []
    }
  ]
}
